Ok.  Well, I'm sort of sick of seeing things like this posted, so 
I finally got around to posting :-).  (Not that this will resolve
the question of 'is there one', but...)

I adapted the telnetd from some BSD UNIX to run any program you wanted;
that way all the curses stuff would work, etc.  If anyone is interested
and willing to wait a month and a half for it, I can redo the adaptation;
I lost the code to it a while ago.

This way, if anyone WANTS to set up a telnet-Nethack, they can.  I would
set one up at Reed if we had better network connections; we have some
free machines, but we really need more bandwidth than we have.

